Pace Chromium's frames by Qt's (Omarchy Mobile).

Chromium took each of its own swaps' start as the display's vsync, so its
frame clock drifted against Qt's frames and doubled up or skipped; and it
could not draw a frame until Qt had taken the previous one (one swap in
flight), which left a 7 ms draw no slack at 120 Hz.

Now the frame is reported as presented at Qt's next frame, which a filtered
phase follows from the times Qt takes frames (QTWEBENGINE_FRAME_PHASE_US
moves Chromium's frame start against it). A swap finishes at once while Qt
keeps up; a frame drawn while Qt still has the previous one waiting replaces
it, and that swap finishes when Qt takes a frame, so a window that is not
drawn stops Chromium after one frame. QTWEBENGINE_FRAME_STATS=1 prints where
presents land relative to Qt's frames.

